14zo|a|One who, or that which, jumps. ; A long drilling tool used by masons and quarrymen. ; A rude kind of sleigh; -- usually, a simple box on runners which are in one piece with the poles that form the thills. ; The larva of the cheese fly. See Cheese fly, under Cheese. ; A name applied in the 18th century to certain Calvinistic Methodists in Wales whose worship was characterized by violent convulsions. ; spring to impel the star wheel, also a pawl to lock fast a wheel, in a repeating timepiece. ; A loose upper garment ; A sort of blouse worn by workmen over their ordinary dress to protect it. ; A fur garment worn in Arctic journeys.	j:awd,111,4;asm,107,6;2b2h,73,5;2b2n,65,3~asm,107,6;2b2h,73,5;awd,111,4;2b2n,65,3
